// Jormangund boss-fight overhaul (wootbeer: "any jewels in your inventory should count down as they are
// added into your score, after that odin's speech should popup again"): this port's own non-blocking
// equivalent of real score_for_inv()'s own jewel-draining half (1_panel.c -- see
// got_boss1_start_jewel_drain()'s own comment for the full real/port comparison), plus the deferred-
// action pattern needed to fix a real, separate pre-existing bug this exposed: got_boss1_closing_
// sequence()'s original code called got_script_execute(1002,...) synchronously, one line after
// got_script_execute(1001,...) -- but got_script_execute() silently no-ops while a script is already
// running (see that function's own reentrancy guard, got_script.c), and script 1001's own dialogue
// box is still open at that point, so the second Odin speech was actually being dropped on the floor
// every single time, never shown. Splitting the closing sequence in two (see got_boss1_closing_
// sequence()/got_boss1_closing_sequence_part2() below) and deferring part 2 until BOTH the jewel
// drain has finished AND got_script_is_running() has gone false fixes both the missing-speech bug
// and gives the jewels their own visible countdown, in the order wootbeer asked for.
static bool s_boss1_jewel_drain_active = false;
static bool s_boss1_jewel_drain_done = false; // drain finished; waiting on got_script_is_running()
											   // to clear before part 2 can actually start
// Jewels still to convert this drain -- captured ONCE, from s_thor.jewels, when the drain starts
// (got_boss1_start_jewel_drain() below), then counted down independently rather than re-reading
// s_thor.jewels on every step. Deliberate: got_thor_add_jewels(-1) (the real per-step `add_jewels
// (-1)` call, see got_boss1_step_jewel_drain()'s own comment) is a no-op while wootbeer's own "unlimited
// jewels" cheat is active (see that function's own gate) -- looping on "while s_thor.jewels>0"
// directly would never terminate under that cheat, silently soft-locking the win sequence (the
// second Odin speech and the bridge reveal both wait on this drain finishing). Counting down a
// separately-captured total guarantees the drain -- and the rest of the closing sequence behind it
// -- always finishes in a fixed number of steps regardless of that cheat's own effect on the actual
// jewel count.
static int s_boss1_jewel_drain_remaining = 0;
static bool s_boss1_jewel_drain_time_inited = false;
static struct timespec s_boss1_jewel_drain_last_time;
static double s_boss1_jewel_drain_phase_ms = 0.0;
// Real score_for_inv()'s own `pause(8)` between each unit drained -- same real ~120Hz timer_cnt
// basis as REVEAL_STEP_MS above (see that constant's own comment for where the 120Hz figure itself
// comes from), just a different real pause-length: 8 real ticks instead of 5.
#define BOSS1_JEWEL_DRAIN_STEP_MS (8000.0 / 120.0)

